  "$comment": "Shared validation corpus. Both runtimes must reach the same verdict on every case: TypeBox Value.Check in packages/contracts/tests/fidelity.test.ts, and the generated Pydantic models in services/worker. Payloads are complete documents so a reader in either language needs no assembly. Each invalid case differs from a valid control in exactly one way, and names the constraint it exercises. Scope: this proves the two runtimes agree on schema CONSTRAINTS. It deliberately contains no type-coercion cases, because Pydantic lax mode converts '5' to 5 where TypeBox rejects it; see the documented coercion divergence in fidelity.test.ts.",
